  "nextGate": "RESIDENT-SOCIAL-MEMORY-01 with bounded POI perception, one source-backed routine interruption/resume, motivation-backed AIDA selection, Lean Memory, ChatterBox/Triplet, Fluff-o-lect and Reaction Choreography",
  "userDirections": [
    "Points of Interest include player, NPCs/Residents, Cube Pets, plants/nature, environment/landmarks, resources, props/cards and activity stations.",
    "Routine activity includes fishing, smithing/hammering, patrol, explore and other role-specific work.",
    "KFB AIDA gameplay loop for player and NPCs: attention → curiosity/interest → expectation → interaction → reaction → interpret/remember/update → return/resume/retarget.",
    "Personal goals/motivations drive attention, target selection, routines and non-automatic conflict.",
    "Toy Soldier working character name is Officer Doppel-Denk; first character proof is gift reveal → rifle march/patrol → resident-specific order/disorder POI interpretation → reaction/retort → clean patrol resume.",
    "All Residents/characters are music-positive; provide a shared beat-driven Common Bounce plus one learnable Signature Dance Move per Resident, with player discovery/learning stored through Player Journey rather than a second skill inventory.",
    "Gift-giving is a shared Resident culture mechanic: source-proven wrapped presents can contain real bizarre/satirical props, trigger character-specific reactions, barter/regifting, bounded prank/failure spirals and later reconciliation while preserving Kayfabe and ownership provenance.",
    "KISS correction: Gift Culture MVP persists meaningful social/emotional receipts, not a durable Resident item economy, barter ledger, per-prop ownership chain or exhaustive gift provenance. Real item tracking is optional future integration only.",
    "Every Resident may have a Signature Deck or cluster that shapes worldview, ChatterBox language and Card POI salience; a Resident may want missing Cards recovered, confiscated, destroyed, archived or otherwise pursued. Deliberate archetype/deck mismatch is valid."
  ],
